---
import CommunityLayout from '../components/CommunityLayout.astro';
import { PAGE_TOOLS } from '../lib/tools';
---

<CommunityLayout
  title="About iDuckConvert: who runs it, what it costs, how it is built"
  description="iDuckConvert is a free set of converters that run in your browser. Learn who runs it, what it costs and how your files are handled."
  before="About"
  mark="iDuckConvert"
  intro={`${PAGE_TOOLS.length} free converters that run in your browser, from the makers of iDuckPDF and iDuckIMG.`}
>
  <section class="card p-5" aria-labelledby="files">
    <h2 id="files" class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight">What happens to your files</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
      Every tool runs in your browser. Your files are opened, changed and saved on your own device, and they are not
      uploaded to our servers. Our host, Cloudflare, sees the same ordinary web requests for our pages that any website
      sees. Please do not rely on that alone for anything truly secret: check any tool you trust, and close the tab when you
      are done.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card p-5" aria-labelledby="who">
    <h2 id="who" class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight">Who runs it</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
      iDuckConvert is made and run by Basic App Company. It is a sister site of
      <a class="link" href="https://iduckpdf.com/" rel="noopener">iDuckPDF</a>, which has free PDF tools, and <a class="link" href="https://iduckimg.com/" rel="noopener">iDuckIMG</a>, which has free image tools, and <a class="link" href="https://iduckcalculator.com/" rel="noopener">iDuckCalculator</a>, which has free calculators, and shares their look. PDF conversions live on iDuckPDF and picture conversions that already exist on iDuckIMG are linked, not copied.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card p-5" aria-labelledby="cost">
    <h2 id="cost" class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight">What it costs</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
      Nothing. There is no sign-up and no watermark on your results. We may show ads to cover the running costs, and we will
      keep them away from the upload area and the download button. See <a class="link" href="/donate/">Donate</a> for ways
      to help.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card p-5" aria-labelledby="built">
    <h2 id="built" class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight">How it is built</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
      The pages are plain static files made with Astro, with small Preact pieces for the tools. Audio and video use ffmpeg.wasm, a copy of ffmpeg compiled to WebAssembly. Its engine file (about 30 MB) is fetched once from a public CDN and then cached by your browser; your files are never sent there. Spreadsheets use SheetJS, and the rest is small open-source code running on your device. Because everything runs on your device, big videos can be slow on an older phone.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card p-5" aria-labelledby="contact">
    <h2 id="contact" class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight">Get in touch</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
      The easiest way is the <a class="link" href="/feedback/">feedback form</a>. To ask for a tool, use
      <a class="link" href="/request/">Request a feature</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</CommunityLayout>
